---
// promptanddone.com/chief — the CHIEF pack (DM deliverable for the "claude-chief-of-staff" reel).
import PackLayout from '../layouts/PackLayout.astro';
const install = 'npx skills@latest add mattpocock/skills --skill chief-of-staff';
const goal = "/chief-of-staff Goal: build me a prompt library web app I'll actually use every day. Save my best AI prompts as cards with tags, search them instantly, fill in {{variables}} before copying, one tap to copy. Everything stays in localStorage and works offline. Mobile-first, dark, premium-looking UI. Plain HTML, CSS and ES modules, no build step. Logic tested with node:test. Seed it with 8 genuinely useful prompts and write a README.";
---
<PackLayout title="Chief of Staff: one goal, a team of agents — Prompt &amp; Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · CHIEF pack</p>
      <h1>One goal to Claude, a team of agents builds it</h1>
      <p class="tag">Chief of Staff is a free (MIT) Claude Code skill by Matt Pocock, in the beta (in-progress) part of his skills repo. Claude hands the work to background subagents, keeps talking to you while they build, and improves the setup (rules, checks, docs) for the next task.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">1</span> Install (in your project)</h2><pre><code>{install}</code></pre>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/blob/main/skills/in-progress/chief-of-staff/SKILL.md">Read the skill on GitHub</a> (it is a short prompt file; the work is real). Beta: it can change without warning.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">2</span> Run it so the agents really go to the background</h2>
      <p>Start an interactive session with <code>claude</code> (not <code>claude -p</code>: one-shot mode runs subagents in the foreground), then type <code>/chief-of-staff</code> and your goal. The agents show up in the panel under the prompt, and you can keep asking questions while they work.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">3</span> The exact goal from the reel</h2><pre><code>{goal}</code></pre></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">4</span> What our run did (17 Oct 2026)</h2>
      <p>Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code: 9 background agents (never more than 3 at once), about 50 minutes, 278 passing tests, a working offline app after 23 minutes. Mid-run it answered an unrelated question in 3.9 seconds while two agents kept building. It also wrote ARCHITECTURE.md, CODING_STANDARDS.md and an <code>npm run check</code> that blocks shortcuts.</p>
      <p>Cost: about $16 at API list prices (we were on a Max plan). To keep it cheaper: use Sonnet, give it a smaller goal, or tell it to skip extra QA rounds.</p></section>
  </main>
</PackLayout>
